Short:    Can't Stop dice board game clone
Author:   Philipp Lonke
Uploader: amiga@lonke.de (Philipp Lonke)
Type:     game/board
Version:  2.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0
Requires: driver/audio/ahiusr_4.18.lha
Kurz:     Klon des Wuerfelspiels Can't Stop

Can't Stop 2.0
==============

A clone of Sid Sackson's classic push-your-luck dice board game
"Can't Stop", written in Hollywood. One to four players (hotseat)
race to the top of the board's columns - including computer
opponents with a risk-aware AI.

Be the first to claim three columns! Each turn you roll four dice,
combine them into two pairs and advance up to three white runners
on the columns 2-12. After every roll you may push your luck and
roll again - or bank your progress and end the turn. If no pairing
can be played, you BUST and lose everything gained this turn.


Features
--------

- Official board layout (column lengths 3-5-7-9-11-13-11-9-7-5-3)
  and the original pairing rules, including the obligation to move
  both sums of a chosen pairing whenever possible
- 1-4 players in any mix of humans and computer opponents
- Computer AI that never banks while a runner is still free,
  secures finished columns and otherwise stops based on the real
  bust probability
- Bust-risk indicator: the exact chance (in %) that your next
  roll busts
- German and English, switchable in the start menu
- Pixel-art title screen, animated dice, flicker-free runner
  sprites, dice-rattle and other sound effects in native 8SVX
- Mouse-driven interface; right mouse button doubles as the main
  action button, ESC returns to the menu


Requirements
------------

- Amiga with 68020 CPU or better, AmigaOS 3.x
- RTG graphics board (Picasso96 or CyberGraphX) required - the game
  opens an 810 x 555 hi/truecolour screen and does NOT run on plain
  AGA/ECS chipset modes
- AHI audio system installed (see Requires)
- Runs on real hardware and in emulation (WinUAE, AmiKit etc.)


Installation
------------

Extract the archive anywhere and double-click the icon. Keep
cantstop68k.info next to the program: apart from the MagicWB and
OS3.5+ colour icon it carries the NOLEGACYAUDIO tooltype, which
selects Hollywood's new AHI audio driver. Without it there is no
sound in AHI-over-emulation setups such as AmiKit/WinUAE. When
starting from a Shell, pass -nolegacyaudio instead.


History
-------

2.0 (08-Aug-2026)  Selectable computer AI strength (easy/normal/strong,
                   verified by simulation). Casino-felt playfield with a
                   gold trim frame and reworked panel layout. Improved
                   player colour contrast on the felt background. Program
                   version shown on the rules screen. Fixed AI-generated
                   artifacts on the title screen dice.
1.0 (23-Jul-2026)  First public release.


Credits
-------

Game design: Sid Sackson (Can't Stop, 1980).
Programming and graphics: Philipp Lonke.
Written in Hollywood (https://www.hollywood-mal.com/).
Source and releases: https://github.com/phipslk/cantstop

This game is freeware. Have fun - and know when to stop!


